{
  "$description": "UX-21 (PLAN_V2_1_POLISH 3b): every command once, for every menu (the Mac menu bar, right-click menus, a row's ⋯, Record's menu, the avatar's menu, ⌘K, the menu-bar and tray menu, the Dock menu, the Windows Jump List). Labels are in sentence case; the Mac's Title Case is made from them (registry.ts, with the words in titleCase). '…' means the command asks for more before it acts. appliesTo: what it works on (none, one, many, oneOrMany). when: the states it needs (registry.ts CONDITIONS); greyed in the menu bar, left out of right-click menus. native: a Tauri predefined menu item (macOS draws and runs it). state: a label or a tick that follows the app (on: the label while the state is on; check: ticked while on). Android uses the same ids and labels.",
  "titleCase": {
    "lower": ["a", "an", "and", "as", "at", "but", "by", "for", "from", "in", "into", "of", "on", "or", "the", "to", "via", "with"],
    "keep": ["EchoLedger", "Live Assist", "Live Translate", "Urdu", "Roman Urdu", "PDF", "WhatsApp"]
  },
